Save93 equipment runs with the test control "skip blocked" (VMCatchUp::SetSkipBlocked) after the review fixes, 2026-11-10 22:46 build / AE 1.6.1170 / limiter 30 FPS, DynamicUpdateBudget=false / Papyrus bEnableLogging=0, bEnableProfiling=1
Test DLL APBGameplayTrace.dll sha256 972440fc6cc62fabbb0c51519e28e11f52027ebeb2e0f34dc61ab827b311ec90 (release DLL of the same source 30e58cbb..., which never calls the control). APB_CATCHUP_MODE=accelerate, target 60, engage below 50, reviewed-read rule with property reads.
The 22:46 build is the 20:58 build (order restoration after a skip cycle fixed, see README "20:58 수정") plus one counter, order_rebuilds: extra cycles after which the linked queue had to be rebuilt because the calls the cycle moved behind were not its front in the order they were moved. The 20:58 build itself was never run in game.
  skfx-30-1, skfx-30-2   catchup-ab with -SkipBlocked: "on" = catch-up on with skip blocked, "off" = catch-up off. Same procedure as skab-30-1, skab-30-2 of the 18:42 build (Save93-VMCatchUp-SkipBlocked-AB.log).
First in-game runs of the fixed restore code. No crash while the trials ran; guard_violations and overrun_pauses 0 in all 16 trials; no "turned off" warning (the queue took every call back); handler counts as in the other runs (174 or 202-203); foreground_pct 100.0 in all 16. One trial matched 11 of 12 equipment requests within 250 ms (skfx-30-2 trial 3); 16 trials of earlier runs show the same, with catch-up off as well.
Closing the game left the known exit crash both times (execute at 0x7FF67B580000, stack through the input hooks of other mods, no module of this project), as every measurement run does.

RESULT, order restoration: the queue was rebuilt after 6 of 1,902 skip cycles (per skip trial 2, 1, 0, 0 / 0, 1, 2, 0); after the others the moved calls were already the front of the queue in their order. So the case the review found does occur in this scene, rarely. That the rebuilt order is the intended one is covered by the unit tests of src/QueueOrder.h only; no log of this run shows the queue content.
RESULT, drain of the equipment handlers (ms after the last signal; same handler count):
  174 handlers: off 1324, 1325, 1356 (3 trials, mean 1335) / on+skip 289, 323, 390, 422 (4 trials, mean 356, -73%). 18:42 build: -75%.
  202-203 handlers: off 1954-2023 (5 trials, mean 2001) / on+skip 655, 688, 759, 959 (4 trials, mean 765, -62%). 18:42 build: -57%.
RESULT, queue wait of every queued native call of every script (below): catch-up off 36.1 and 36.4 ms / on+skip 22.4 and 24.8 ms (-38%, -32%); same-frame share 9% -> 36%. 18:42 build: 33.8 and 39.9 / 24.9 and 22.4.
COST: extra time per frame 0.12-0.14 ms; largest single frame 1.06 ms (18:42 build 0.97); an extra cycle ran in 237-238 of 239 frames; 944-1378 calls moved behind per trial. Engine frame time p99 35.60-35.64 off / 35.78-36.04 on. Utility.Wait response p95 59.4-59.6 off / 59.8-60.5 on.
READING: the effect is the same as before the fix within the spread of these trials; the fix did not cost it. Not repeated on this build: skip against the release rule in the same launch (catchup-skipfront), 42 FPS, the quest rehearsal.

